{"task_id": "task_32075f4ef5", "session_id": "eval-dsa_lis-r0", "timestamp": "2026-10-06T19:31:11", "tool": "agent", "action": "run", "arguments": "{\"task\": \"Using Python, compute the length of the longest strictly increasing subsequence of [10,9,2,5,3,7,101,18]. Show the code and the answer.\"}", "risk_level": "low", "permission": "not_required", "result": "To solve this problem using Python, we can use dynamic programming to find the length of the longest strictly increasing subsequence (LIS). Here's how you could implement it:\n\n```python\ndef lis_length(nums):\n    if not nums:\n        return 0\n    \n    dp = [1] * len(nums)\n    \n    for i in range(1, len(nums)):\n        for j in range(i):\n            if nums[i] > nums[j]:\n                dp[i] = max(dp[i], dp[j] + 1)\n                \n    return max(dp)\n\nnums = [10,9,2,5,3,7,101,18]\nprint(lis_length(nums))\n```\n\nNow let's run the code to find the length of the longest strictly increasing subsequence.", "verification": "pass", "duration": 11.4, "error": "", "retry_count": 0}
