{"task_id": "task_006817e1a6", "session_id": "eval-dsa_lis-r0", "timestamp": "2026-10-08T18:40:26", "tool": "code_run", "action": "execute", "arguments": "{\"code\": \"import bisect\\n\\ndef length_of_lis(nums):\\n    sub = []\\n    for x in nums:\\n        idx = bisect.bisect_left(sub, x)\\n        if idx == len(sub):\\n            sub.append(x)\\n        else:\\n            sub[idx] = x\\n    return len(sub)\\n\\nnums = [10, 9, 2, 5, 3, 7, 101, 18]\\nlength = length_of_lis(nums)\\nprint(f\\\"Array: {nums}\\\")\\nprint(f\\\"LIS Length: {length}\\\")\\n\"}", "risk_level": "medium", "permission": "not_required", "result": "{\"command\": \"python\", \"exit_code\": 0, \"output\": \"Array: [10, 9, 2, 5, 3, 7, 101, 18]\\nLIS Length: 4\\n\"}", "verification": "unverified", "duration": 0.0, "error": "", "retry_count": 0}
{"task_id": "task_006817e1a6", "session_id": "eval-dsa_lis-r0", "timestamp": "2026-10-08T18:40:30", "tool": "agent", "action": "run", "arguments": "{\"task\": \"Using Python, compute the length of the longest strictly increasing subsequence of [10,9,2,5,3,7,101,18]. Show the code and the answer.\"}", "risk_level": "low", "permission": "not_required", "result": "The length of the longest strictly increasing subsequence is **4** (for example, `[2, 3, 7, 101]` or `[2, 5, 7, 18]`).\n\n### Python Code ($O(N \\log N)$ Patience Sorting / Binary Search)\n\n```python\nimport bisect\n\ndef length_of_lis(nums: list[int]) -> int:\n    sub = []\n    for num in nums:\n        idx = bisect.bisect_left(sub, num)\n        if idx == len(sub):\n            sub.append(num)\n        else:\n            sub[idx] = num\n    return len(sub)\n\nnums = [10, 9, 2, 5, 3, 7, 101, 18]\nresult = length_of_lis(nums)\nprint(f\"Length of LIS: {result}\")\n```\n\n### Output\n```text\nLength of LIS: 4\n```", "verification": "unverified", "duration": 30.6, "error": "", "retry_count": 0}
