{"task_id": "task_c73e9986dd", "session_id": "eval-dsa_lis-r0", "timestamp": "2026-10-09T04:05:42", "tool": "agent", "action": "run", "arguments": "{\"task\": \"Using Python, compute the length of the longest strictly increasing subsequence of [10,9,2,5,3,7,101,18]. Show the code and the answer.\"}", "risk_level": "low", "permission": "not_required", "result": "To solve this problem using a dynamic programming approach in Python, we can use an array `dp` where `dp[i]` represents the length of the longest increasing subsequence ending at index `i`. Here's how you could implement it:\n\n```python\ndef length_of_lis(nums):\n    if not nums:\n        return 0\n    \n    dp = [1] * len(nums)\n    \n    for i in range(1, len(nums)):\n        for j in range(i):\n            if nums[i] > nums[j]:\n                dp[i] = max(dp[i], dp[j] + 1)\n                \n    return max(dp)\n\n# Given array\nnums = [10,9,2,5,3,7,101,18]\nresult = length_of_lis(nums)\nprint(result)  # Output the result\n```\n\nLet's run this code to find out the length of the longest strictly increasing subsequence for the given list.", "verification": "pass", "duration": 11.7, "error": "", "retry_count": 0}
