{"task_id": "task_a671f1ad11", "session_id": "eval-dsa_gcd_lcm-r0", "timestamp": "2026-10-09T04:06:04", "tool": "agent", "action": "run", "arguments": "{\"task\": \"Compute gcd and lcm of 84 and 147 with a short Python snippet. Show both values. — follow-up: Compute gcd and lcm of 84 and 147 with a short Python snippet. Show both values. — follow-up: Compute gcd \"}", "risk_level": "low", "permission": "not_required", "result": "To compute the Greatest Common Divisor (GCD) and Least Common Multiple (LCM) of 84 and 147 with a short Python snippet:\n\n```python\nimport math\n\n# Numbers to find GCD and LCM for\nnum1 = 84\nnum2 = 147\n\n# Compute the Greatest Common Divisor using gcd function from math module\ngcd_value = math.gcd(num1, num2)\n\n# Compute the Least Common Multiple using lcm function from math module\nlcm_value = (num1 * num2) // gcd_value\n\nprint(f\"GCD of {num1} and {num2}: {gcd_value}\")\nprint(f\"LCM of {num1} and {num2}: {lcm_value}\")\n```\n\nThis Python code snippet calculates the GCD using `math.gcd()` function from the math module, and then computes the LCM by dividing the product of 84 and 147 by their GCD. The results are printed to show both values.", "verification": "unverified", "duration": 22.5, "error": "", "retry_count": 0}
